Source license notes
--------------------

The FxFloorBoard source files carry GPL version 2 or later headers and the archive ships the
GPL version 3 text as license.txt. midi.xml itself carries an "All rights reserved" line without
an explicit license of its own; it is treated as part of the GPL-licensed program. The derived
data in this crate is distributed under GPL-3.0-or-later together with the rest of Tsuba.
Residual risk: should the copyright holder consider midi.xml separately licensed, the derived
table would have to be replaced with independently researched data.

Changes made to the derived data
--------------------------------

* Addresses, sizes, ranges and labels were converted into a flat JSON table (704 parameters).
* patch_size corrected from 3912 to 1992 (RQ1 size 00 00 0F 48, as measured on the amp).
* The variant_select_values table was removed; type/variant linkage lives in tsuba-protocol.
* Contour Freq Shift was moved from the unused byte 06 1A to the per-contour slots 0F 31, 0F 39
  and 0F 41, and Contour Shape (0F 30, 0F 38, 0F 40) was added, matching the FxFloorBoard UI
  (stompbox_cab.cpp). Contour Select options are labelled Contour 1 to Contour 3.
* Each entry is tagged "research" ([R], taken from FxFloorBoard) unless it was verified on a real
  Katana 50 MK II ([V], with the verification date).
* Sixteen entries that BOSS TONE STUDIO for KATANA MkII 2.1.0 keeps hidden and fixed
  (address_map.js entries without a name) are marked "hidden" and locked to the official
  values: 00 23 Preamp 10, 00 2A Gain SW 1, 00 36 and 00 37 Bass/Treble Freq 0 to 10, and for
  MOD (02 xx) and FX (04 xx) 0F Separ 0, 17 RT Speed 1, 1A and 1B RT Rise/Fall Time 0,
  28 VB Off/On 1, 29 VB Rise Time 0. Hidden entries are not shown and not written one by one.
* Delay types 3 to 5 (Dual series, Dual parallel, Dual L/R) and reverb types 0 and 2 (Ambience,
  Hall1) were removed from the type choices at 05 01, 05 21, 05 41 and the variant types
  06 2D to 06 35, and the remaining choices follow the official menu order.
* The chain slots 06 00 to 06 13 are marked hidden. The official editor treats them as padding
  and sets the signal chain only through the CHAIN pattern at 06 20 (0 to 6).
* data/official_ranges.json lists the official raw range of every Temporary patch byte
  (60 00 xx xx) from BOSS TONE STUDIO 2.1.0 address_map.js, as page, byte, size, min, max.
  Full patch writes normalise fixed values and reject any other value outside these ranges.
